From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bindings: use nixl-sys stub API on riscv64

dynamo-llm (block-manager, on by default) and dynamo-memory pull in
nixl-sys 1.3.2. Its build.rs is meant to fall back to a dlopen stub API
when NIXL is not installed - which is how upstream's own wheel is built
("sans nixl") - but build_nixl() calls get_arch() before it looks for
libnixl.so, and get_arch() panics on anything but x86_64/aarch64:

    panicked at build.rs: Unsupported architecture: riscv64

A panic is not the Err that triggers the stub fallback, so the build
dies on riscv64. Requesting nixl-sys's `stub-api` feature skips
build_nixl() entirely and compiles the same stubs upstream's wheel
ships. It is scoped to riscv64 so other targets are unchanged; the
proper fix is for nixl-sys's get_arch() to stop panicking.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [workaround for nixl-sys get_arch() panicking on riscv64; the real fix belongs in ai-dynamo/nixl]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
diff --git a/lib/bindings/python/Cargo.lock b/lib/bindings/python/Cargo.lock
index a87d665..8054f83 100644
--- a/lib/bindings/python/Cargo.lock
+++ b/lib/bindings/python/Cargo.lock
@@ -2404,6 +2404,7 @@ dependencies = [
  "dynamo-vllm-sidecar",
  "dynamo-worker-selection-policy-catalog",
  "futures",
+ "nixl-sys",
  "once_cell",
  "opentelemetry",
  "opentelemetry_sdk",
diff --git a/lib/bindings/python/Cargo.toml b/lib/bindings/python/Cargo.toml
index 414c748..0055d28 100644
--- a/lib/bindings/python/Cargo.toml
+++ b/lib/bindings/python/Cargo.toml
@@ -127,6 +127,10 @@ pythonize = "0.23"
 [target.'cfg(target_os = "linux")'.dependencies]
 dynamo-llm = { path = "../../llm" }
 
+# nixl-sys's build.rs only knows x86_64/aarch64 and panics before its stub fallback.
+[target.'cfg(target_arch = "riscv64")'.dependencies]
+nixl-sys = { version = "=1.3.2", features = ["stub-api"] }
+
 [target.'cfg(not(target_os = "linux"))'.dependencies]
 dynamo-llm = { path = "../../llm", default-features = false }
 
